  <h2 id="budget">How much of your education budget this actually deserves</h2>

  <p>
    Treat any single course on this page as a rough 10 percent slice of your family's total realistic
    education budget, not the whole pie. If the complete education budget is Rs 10 lakh, that starting
    benchmark leaves roughly Rs 1 lakh for the course itself and about Rs 9 lakh available for living
    costs, tools, internet access, books, coaching if genuinely needed, and future upskilling.
  </p>

  <p class="note-line">
    This is a strict planning heuristic, not a universal rule. Spending materially more can make sense
    when a specific institute or coaching programme has a verifiable, checkable advantage: real
    placement data, named recruiters, or a demonstrably better pass rate for CA, CS, or CMA coaching,
    not the institute's brand alone.
  </p>

  <p>
    Most commerce degrees and all three professional qualifications comfortably fit inside that
    heuristic. The place students actually overspend is expensive, unverified "guaranteed placement"
    coaching add-ons and premium private colleges with no checkable outcome data. That is where to apply
    real scrutiny before signing a cheque or taking a loan.
  </p>

